  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong, moderate-cost multimodal baseline to anchor the search. config_008 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities with multiprofile aggregation improves accuracy, while using well-established, cheaper components (PCA for RNA, ResNet50 for images, avgpool for aggregation) to keep training cost low (~30-40% of a ViT-L + scgpt + transformer config). This gives a reliable performance reference point: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can selectively upgrade individual components (e.g., swap to ViT-L or scgpt) to identify which upgrades matter most; if it underperforms, it signals that the multimodal combination strategy itself needs rethinking. Choosing a mid-cost configuration first preserves GPU budget for the 9 remaining experiments while still providing a strong signal about the multimodal design space."
}

